// Search index for the wiki search box. Generated by tools/build.py; don't edit by hand.
window.RC_SEARCH=[{"p":"Order & Chaos","h":"Order & Chaos","u":"alignment.html","x":"Civic alignment on Republic City MC: how Order and Chaos are earned and what they lead to. Like Raava and Vaatu, two forces pull at Republic City. Your choices earn Order or Chaos : two separate meters, so earning one never costs you the other. At a glance Two meters Order and Chaos, counted separately Earned by Story choices and some side quests See yours On your dossier Why it matters It decides which roleplay ranks will take you Contents How It Works Choices in Arc 1 Why It Matters"},{"p":"Order & Chaos","h":"How It Works","u":"alignment.html#how","x":"Order Chaos You earn it by Playing it straight: reporting, cooperating, handing over evidence Leverage: threats, bribes, keeping what you find In Arc 1 Turn Ren in the right way; hand Aang everything Squeeze Ren for his silence; pocket the ring Leads to Police, United Forces, White Lotus, Kyoshi Warriors Street gangs, the Red Lotus, the Ungiven Your dossier shows which way you lean, with both totals."},{"p":"Order & Chaos","h":"Choices in Arc 1","u":"alignment.html#arc1","x":"When Order Chaos Quest 7: squeezing Ren +5 Order +5 Chaos and 30 Yuans hush money Arc 1 finale: the ring +10 Order +10 Chaos, and you keep the ring Kept the ring? After Arc 1, Shady Zhen will buy it once for 125 Yuans and another 5 Chaos. Side quest choices Side quest Order Chaos Special Delivery Deliver Ren's envelope sealed: +2 Order Break the seal and read it: +2 Chaos Scoop! Print the plain truth: +2 Order Run the monster headline: +2 Chaos"},{"p":"Order & Chaos","h":"Why It Matters","u":"alignment.html#why","x":"Alignment decides which roleplay ranks will have you, and how the city's people treat you in later arcs."},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"Bending & Tiers","u":"bending.html","x":"How bending tiers, Quest Points, paths and tier bonuses work on Republic City MC. Every path starts at Tier I and climbs to Tier ★. You climb by earning Quest Points and passing your trainer's exam. Each tier keeps everything before it. At a glance Tiers I → II → III → ★, and you keep everything you learn To climb Quest Points plus your trainer's exam (Tier II exams are coming soon) At Tier III Choose one path. It's permanent. QP in Arc 1 About 41 from the story, about 14 more from side quests Contents Paths The Four Tiers Every Tier Hits Harder Tier III Paths Discipline Technique Scrolls"},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"Paths","u":"bending.html#elements","x":"Earthbending Metal or Lava Waterbending Ice, Healing and Plants Firebending Lightning or Combustion Chi Blocking Equalist or Kyoshi Warrior Weapons Master Any blade, no bending You pick your path on your Registration Form, and it's permanent. Each path's page lists its moves at every tier, its trainers and the roleplay ranks open to it."},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"The Four Tiers","u":"bending.html#tiers","x":"Tier To unlock What you get I · Forms Where everyone starts Your starting moves, already on your hotbar II · Street 50 QP + your trainer's exam coming soon Crowd control, defense and your first combos III · Master 250 QP + a boss fight Master moves, and you choose one path ★ · Legend 500 QP + a duel with a legend, then a feat Your path's signature move Quest Points (QP) are your service record. You earn them from the main story (about 41 in Arc 1) and side quests (about 14 more). They're never spent, traded or sold."},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"Every Tier Hits Harder","u":"bending.html#stronger","x":"On top of new moves, each tier boosts the moves you already have: Tier Damage Cooldowns Range Charge time I — — — — II +10% −5% +5% −5% III +20% −10% +10% −10% ★ +30% −15% +15% −15% Speed, height, knockback and area never change, so a higher tier is an edge, not a one-shot."},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"Tier III Paths","u":"bending.html#paths","x":"At Tier III your trainer's quest lets you choose one path. It's permanent, and it leads to your ★ signature move. Path Tier III paths ★ signature Earthbending Metal · Lava Lava Flow (Lava) · Metal: coming later Waterbending None yet: every waterbender learns ice, healing and plants Water Arms Firebending Lightning · Combustion Coming later Chi Blocking Equalist · Kyoshi Warrior Coming later Weapons Master Coming later Coming later"},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"Discipline","u":"bending.html#discipline","x":"Your dossier shows your Discipline under your element: your Tier III path, or the bending styles your tier has opened (Sand for earthbenders, Ice · Healing · Plant for waterbenders, both from Tier II)."},{"p":"Bending & Tiers","h":"Technique Scrolls","u":"bending.html#scrolls","x":"Rare boss drops that teach one move early, for good. Right-click to read one. The wrong path can't read it, but can sell it. The first is Scroll: Catapult from Pitmaster Jax, for earthbenders."},{"p":"Chi Blocking","h":"Chi Blocking","u":"chi-blocking.html","x":"Chi blocking on Republic City MC: abilities by tier, the Equalist and Kyoshi Warrior paths, trainers and ranks. Chi Blocking Type Non-bender Style Speed and pressure points: shut a bender down Paths Equalist or Kyoshi Warrior (Tier III) Trainers Acrobat Lee · Ty Lee · Suki Ranks Kyoshi Warriors, The Ungiven Chi blockers don't bend. They strike the body's chi paths to stop a bender cold, and they're fast enough to get there first. Ty Lee made the art famous. In 130 AG more non-benders are learning it, and not all of them agree on why. Contents Abilities Paths Trainers Roleplay Ranks Tips"},{"p":"Chi Blocking","h":"Abilities","u":"chi-blocking.html#abilities","x":"Tier Abilities I · Forms Quick Strike, Swift Kick, Acrobat Stance, High Jump II · Street Rapid Punch, Paralyze, Smokescreen, Bola III · Master Your path's moves ★ · Legend Your path's signature What each tier needs: Bending & Tiers ."},{"p":"Chi Blocking","h":"Paths","u":"chi-blocking.html#paths","x":"At Tier III, choose one. It's permanent. Equalist The early days of a movement that says bending makes some citizens more equal than others. No masks, no leader yet: just people with a grievance. Tier III: Immobilize combo ★: Shock Glove coming later Kyoshi Warrior Fans, armor and discipline, in the tradition of Avatar Kyoshi and Suki. Tier III: Warrior Stance ★: coming later"},{"p":"Chi Blocking","h":"Trainers","u":"chi-blocking.html#trainers","x":"Tier Trainer II Acrobat Lee Endurance and acrobatics, high above the street. Exam coming soon. III Ty Lee Pressure points and agility. ★ Suki Kyoshi Warrior leader."},{"p":"Chi Blocking","h":"Roleplay Ranks","u":"chi-blocking.html#ranks","x":"Kyoshi Warriors (Order): chi blockers and weapons masters only. Tier II and 50 Order. The Ungiven (Chaos): chi blockers and weapons masters only. Tier II. Plus the ranks open to every path. See Roleplay Ranks ."},{"p":"Chi Blocking","h":"Tips","u":"chi-blocking.html#tips","x":"Acrobat Stance and High Jump make you hard to pin down: stay mobile and pick your moment. Bola (Tier II) wraps a target and slows them, which sets up everything else."},{"p":"Commands","h":"Commands","u":"commands.html","x":"Every player command on Republic City MC. Everything you can type in game. Your Welcome to Republic City pamphlet has the basics too. At a glance Most used /quests · /dossier · /wp · /b display Going home /apartment Need staff /helpop <message> Contents Bending Your Dossier Getting Around Talking to People"},{"p":"Commands","h":"Bending","u":"commands.html#bending","x":"Command What it does /b display Lists every ability you can use right now. /b help <ability> Explains an ability and how to use it. /b bind <ability> <slot> Puts an ability on a hotbar slot (1–9). /b toggle Turns your bending off and on."},{"p":"Commands","h":"Your Dossier","u":"commands.html#records","x":"Command What it does /dossier [name] Your official record, or someone else's. Crouch + right-click a player also works. See Dossier & Titles . /quests Your quest log: main story and side quests, rewards, and which one your compass follows. /achievements [name] Achievements earned. /titles Pick the title you wear. /bal Your Yuans."},{"p":"Commands","h":"Getting Around","u":"commands.html#getting-around","x":"Command What it does /wp Fast travel to any waypoint you've discovered. /backpack Quest items that didn't fit, or that you had when you died. /apartment Go home, or step back outside. More in Housing ."},{"p":"Commands","h":"Talking to People","u":"commands.html#talking","x":"Command What it does /msg <name> <text> Private message. /r replies. /mail Leave a letter for someone who's offline. /helpop <text> Reach city staff. /rules The full ordinances."},{"p":"Crafting","h":"Crafting","u":"crafting.html","x":"How crafting works on Republic City MC: learning recipes, Scrap Lessons and blueprints. Public crafting tables stand all over the Civic District, but you have to learn a recipe before you can craft it. Vanilla Minecraft recipes work as normal. At a glance The rule Learn a recipe before you can craft it Start here Old Man Shen's Scrap Lessons Better gear Blueprints from TenTen and epic hidden caches Vanilla recipes Work as normal Contents Learning the Basics Blueprints Every Recipe"},{"p":"Crafting","h":"Learning the Basics","u":"crafting.html#basics","x":"Ask Old Man Shen (market by the Sparring Grounds) about crafting. That starts the Scrap Lessons side quest: he gives you 12 bamboo and teaches the basic recipes. Bamboo Bundle Scrap Steel Ingot Training Staff Arrows, Bow and Shield Concealed Dagger Smoke Bomb"},{"p":"Crafting","h":"Blueprints","u":"crafting.html#blueprints","x":"Better gear comes from blueprints. Right-click one to learn its recipe for good; the blueprint is used up, and its description shows the recipe. Blueprint Where Simple Jian, Dao, Gaff Hook TenTen, 40 Yuans each (Weapons Masters only) Simple Maul TenTen, 60 Yuans (Weapons Masters only) Spider Fang Dagger Epic hidden caches"},{"p":"Crafting","h":"Every Recipe","u":"crafting.html#recipes","x":"Ingredients, effects and prices for every item are in the Field Guide ."},{"p":"Dossier & Titles","h":"Dossier & Titles","u":"dossier.html","x":"Your official record on Republic City MC: what the dossier shows, achievements and titles. The Hall of Civic Records keeps a dossier on every citizen. Anyone can read it, so it's how people know who you are. Open it with /dossier , or right-click your Registration Form or Citizenship Papers. At a glance Open yours /dossier , or right-click your papers Read someone's Crouch + right-click them, or /dossier <name> Wear a title /titles Contents Opening a Dossier What It Shows Achievements and Titles"},{"p":"Dossier & Titles","h":"Opening a Dossier","u":"dossier.html#opening","x":"Crouch and right-click another player, or type /dossier <name> . They have to be online. On your own dossier, the bottom row opens your Quest Log ( /quests ), Titles and Travel Map ( /wp )."},{"p":"Dossier & Titles","h":"What It Shows","u":"dossier.html#contents","x":"Entry What it means Name and title Your character's name (username in brackets) and the title you wear. Service Record Your Quest Points. Next Tier How many Quest Points your next bending tier needs, and how close you are. Legal Status Unregistered, Registration Filed, or Registered Citizen. Click it for achievements. Place of Origin From your Registration Form. Bending Your path, your Discipline (Tier III path, or the styles your tier has opened) and your Mastery (I, II, III or ★). See Bending & Tiers . Roleplay Rank Your group, or Unaffiliated. See Roleplay Ranks . Civic Alignment Your Order and Chaos totals. See Order & Chaos . Purse Your Yuans."},{"p":"Dossier & Titles","h":"Achievements and Titles","u":"dossier.html#titles","x":"Each achievement unlocks a title. Wear one at a time with /titles ; it shows on your dossier. The Arc 1 achievements are listed on the Main Story page."},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"Earthbending","u":"earthbending.html","x":"Earthbending on Republic City MC: abilities by tier, which earth you can bend, the Metal and Lava paths, trainers and ranks. Earthbending Element Earth Style Substance: stand your ground, strike when it counts Paths Metal or Lava (Tier III) Discipline Sand from Tier II Trainers Young Lin Beifong · Penga · Toph Beifong Gang Terra Triad Earthbenders move rock and soil. In 130 AG the city is built by them: Public Works hires earthbenders, and Chief Toph Beifong's Metalbending Police keep its streets. The purer the earth, the earlier you can bend it. Metal and lava come only with their Tier III paths. Contents Abilities What You Can Bend Paths Trainers Roleplay Ranks Tips"},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"Abilities","u":"earthbending.html#abilities","x":"Tier Abilities I · Forms Earth Blast, Raise Earth, Collapse, Earth Armor II · Street Shockwave, Earth Grab, Earth Smash, Catapult, Earth Tunnel, Tremorsense, Earth Dome combo III · Master Earth Pillars combo , plus your path's moves ★ · Legend Your path's signature Combos are performed by chaining other moves; /b help <combo> shows the sequence. What each tier needs: Bending & Tiers ."},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"What You Can Bend","u":"earthbending.html#earth","x":"From tier Earth I Dirt, coarse dirt, grass, podzol, mycelium, rooted dirt, dirt paths, gravel, clay, stone, cobblestone, granite, diorite, andesite II Deepslate, tuff, calcite, dripstone, mud, packed mud, terracotta, sand, red sand, sandstone III Ore veins (coal, lapis, redstone, diamond, emerald), coal blocks, amethyst, netherrack, basalt, blackstone ★ Worked stone: stone bricks, smooth and polished stone, the city's paving, ancient debris Earth that's too impure for you won't move, and you'll see \"This earth is too impure for you to bend yet.\" Bent earth always settles back where it was."},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"Paths","u":"earthbending.html#paths","x":"At Tier III, choose one. It's permanent. Metal Toph Beifong's own invention, and the badge of her police force. Metalbenders sense the bits of earth left in refined metal. Tier III: Metal Clips, Extraction ★: Metal Cables coming later Bends: iron, gold and copper, ore and block Lava Rare and feared. Lavabenders melt earth into magma and turn it back to stone. Tier III: Magma Shot, Lava Manipulation ★: Lava Flow, earned by a feat"},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"Trainers","u":"earthbending.html#trainers","x":"Tier Trainer II Young Lin Beifong Toph's daughter. Exam coming soon. III Penga One of Toph's first metalbending students. ★ Toph Beifong Founder of metalbending."},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"Roleplay Ranks","u":"earthbending.html#ranks","x":"Terra Triad (Chaos): the earthbender gang. Tier I and 25 Chaos to join. Plus the ranks open to every path: police, United Forces, White Lotus, Red Lotus and Cabbage Corp. See Roleplay Ranks ."},{"p":"Earthbending","h":"Tips","u":"earthbending.html#tips","x":"Scroll: Catapult from Pitmaster Jax teaches Catapult before Tier II. Earth Armor and Raise Earth need earth nearby: fight near stone and soil, not on brick. Tremorsense (Tier II) lets you feel the ground around you: handy in the dark sewers."},{"p":"Money & Shops","h":"Money & Shops","u":"economy.html","x":"Yuans, Quest Points, the shops of the Civic District and the daily hidden caches. Republic City runs on Yuans . Your Quest Points are your service record and can't be bought. Nothing for sale makes you stronger. At a glance Money Yuans. Check with /bal Earn it Quests, wallets from human enemies, daily hidden caches Can't buy Quest Points, or anything that makes you stronger Spend it TenTen, Raku, Old Man Shen, Jian's Tea House, Landlady Fe Contents Yuans and Quest Points Shops Hidden Caches"},{"p":"Money & Shops","h":"Yuans and Quest Points","u":"economy.html#currency","x":"Yuans Quest Points What it is Everyday money. Check it with /bal . Your service record. Unlocks bending tiers and roleplay ranks . How to earn Quests (580 across Arc 1), side quests, hidden caches, and wallets dropped by Triad members and police recruits (0–10 Yuans; more from a fleeing grunt you catch). Quests, side quests and the occasional hidden cache. Spend or trade? Spend at shops, on housing and on name changes. Never spent, traded or sold."},{"p":"Money & Shops","h":"Shops","u":"economy.html#shops","x":"Vendor Where Sells Weapons Vendor TenTen Sparring Grounds Weapons, and blade blueprints for Weapons Masters Noodle Man Raku Ramen truck, Civic Plaza Ramen, skewers, cookies Old Man Shen Market by the Sparring Grounds Scrap and materials. Ask him about crafting . Jian's Tea House Jian's Tea Shop Teas with effects (below). Opens again after Quest 3. Landlady Fe Unity Flats Furniture for your apartment Shady Zhen The back alley Nothing. He buys Triad chits (2), Spider-Rat pelts (1) and Brood Queen chitin (15), no questions asked. Full price lists: Field Guide . Jian's Teas Tea Yuans Effect Spiderbane Oolong 15 Cures poison, then 3 minutes of spider-venom immunity Jasmine 10 Speed for 2 minutes Ginseng 12 Regeneration for 15 seconds Ginger Root 12 Fire resistance for 2 minutes Night Blossom 8 Night vision for 5 minutes White Jade 1 Don't."},{"p":"Money & Shops","h":"Hidden Caches","u":"economy.html#caches","x":"Barrels and chests around the city restock every day at midnight Eastern. A stocked cache glows: green sparkles are common, blue dust rare, purple magic epic. The first person to open one claims it for the day. Take what you want; click the gold Yuan nuggets and Quest Point stars to cash them in. You can claim 3 a day . Inside: Yuans, food, materials, now and then a weapon, Quest Points, or (epic only) a Spider Fang Dagger blueprint or a technique scroll."},{"p":"Mobs, Bosses & Items","h":"Mobs, Bosses & Items","u":"field-guide.html","x":"Every enemy, boss and item in Republic City MC: health, drops, prices and recipes. Every enemy you'll face and every item you'll carry. Blurred rows are spoilers; click one to reveal it. Contents How to Fight Mobs Bosses Items"},{"p":"Mobs, Bosses & Items","h":"How to Fight","u":"field-guide.html#how-to-fight","x":"Watch for the ⚠. Before any special move, an enemy warns you on screen (⚠ winds up an Earth Blast! ) and pauses. That pause is your chance to step aside, jump or back off. Read the health bar. Hit something and a bar appears by its name, green when it's healthy and red when it's nearly down. ★ Veterans. About one enemy in twenty is a Veteran: a gold name, roughly double the health and a harder hit. Beat one and you get a second wallet roll (or extra pelts from a Spider-Rat Soldier). Punish a mistake. A Bruiser who misses his charge is dazed and takes extra damage for a moment. Earthbending recruits hide behind a stone guard; wait it out. Keep an eye on your loot. After a Triad fight, a pickpocket may run in and grab what's on the ground. Catch him and he drops it. Recruits don't fight to the death. At the Sparring Grounds a beaten recruit yields and gives you a tip about their element. It still counts as a win. Bosses scale with your group. The Spider-Rat Queen and Pitmaster Jax get more health for every extra player, and everyone who did at least 10% of the damage gets their own drops."},{"p":"Mobs, Bosses & Items","h":"Mobs","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Name Health Melee Found In Abilities Drops"},{"p":"Mobs, Bosses & Items","h":"Bosses","u":"field-guide.html#bosses","x":"Name Health Melee Found In Abilities Drops"},{"p":"Mobs, Bosses & Items","h":"Items","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Prices are what the vendors charge, in Yuans. Where they are: Money & Shops . Item Price Where to Get Recipe Effect / Notes Requires"},{"p":"Firebending","h":"Firebending","u":"firebending.html","x":"Firebending on Republic City MC: abilities by tier, the Lightning and Combustion paths, trainers and ranks. Firebending Element Fire Style Power: relentless pressure, fire from the breath Paths Lightning or Combustion (Tier III) Sources None needed Trainers Business Man Shinu · Royal Academy Elite · Zuko / Iroh Strongest By day (+25%) Gang Agni Kai Firebenders make their own fire from their breath and chi. No source needed, which makes them the most aggressive path in the city. In 130 AG industry is booming, and firebenders who can run a boiler or a power line are in demand. Contents Abilities Paths Trainers Roleplay Ranks Tips"},{"p":"Firebending","h":"Abilities","u":"firebending.html#abilities","x":"Tier Abilities I · Forms Fire Blast, Blaze, Fire Jet, Heat Control, Illumination II · Street Fire Burst, Fire Shield, Fire Manipulation, Fire Kick combo , Fire Spin combo III · Master Wall of Fire, Jet Blast combo , Jet Blaze combo , Fire Wheel combo , plus your path's moves ★ · Legend Your path's signature Combos are performed by chaining other moves; /b help <combo> shows the sequence. What each tier needs: Bending & Tiers ."},{"p":"Firebending","h":"Paths","u":"firebending.html#paths","x":"At Tier III, choose one. It's permanent. Lightning Cold-blooded fire. In Republic City, lightning-benders are starting to find work in the power plants. Tier III: Lightning ★: Lightning Redirection coming later Combustion Very rare: an explosion focused through the mind. Combustion-benders are feared for good reason. Tier III: Combustion ★: coming later"},{"p":"Firebending","h":"Trainers","u":"firebending.html#trainers","x":"Tier Trainer II Business Man Shinu Out to prove firebending beats coal. Exam coming soon. III Royal Academy Elite Precision lightning and controlled combustion. ★ Fire Lord Zuko / General Iroh The Fire Lord and the Dragon of the West."},{"p":"Firebending","h":"Roleplay Ranks","u":"firebending.html#ranks","x":"Agni Kai (Chaos): the firebender gang. Tier I and 25 Chaos to join. Plus the ranks open to every path: police, United Forces, White Lotus, Red Lotus and Cabbage Corp. See Roleplay Ranks ."},{"p":"Firebending","h":"Tips","u":"firebending.html#tips","x":"Fire Jet is your escape and your gap-closer: keep it bound. Heat Control puts out fires on you, and melts ice and snow in your way. You're 25% stronger by day."},{"p":"Housing","h":"Housing","u":"housing.html","x":"Your own apartment at Unity Flats: getting the key, decorating, roommates and commands. Unity Flats How to get Finish Arc 1 Cost Free, and yours for good Furniture Landlady Fe Command /apartment Finishing Arc 1 earns the key to your own room at Unity Flats. Decorate it, store your things, and sleep in your bed to respawn there. Contents Getting Home Decorating Home Comforts Furniture and Trophies Guests and Roommates"},{"p":"Housing","h":"Getting Home","u":"housing.html#getting-home","x":"Right-click your apartment key, or type /apartment , to go home. Do it again (or use any iron door inside) to step back outside Unity Flats. You can't head home for 10 seconds after taking damage."},{"p":"Housing","h":"Decorating","u":"housing.html#building","x":"You can build and place things inside your room. Walls, floor and ceiling stay as they are. Furniture is sold by Landlady Fe , out front of Unity Flats. Unity Flats is also a /wp waypoint once you've walked past it. Bending, PvP and mobs are switched off in the building."},{"p":"Housing","h":"Home Comforts","u":"housing.html#comforts","x":"Healing at home. While you're in your own room (or one where you're a roommate), you slowly heal. Rest. Right-click your bed for full hunger and a \"Well rested\" note, once every 5 minutes. Sleeping in it also sets your respawn. Whetstone. Place one and right-click it to repair the item in your hand for 10 Yuans. It only works in your own home."},{"p":"Housing","h":"Furniture and Trophies","u":"housing.html#furniture","x":"Landlady Fe sells 17 pieces in a 130 AG style: chairs and cushions, tea tables and a Pai Sho table, paper and stone lanterns, a fire brazier, a folding screen, rugs, a deco lamp, the whetstone and a weapon rack. Right-click the floor or a wall to place a piece; hit it once to pick it back up. Two pieces can't be bought. You earn them: Trophy How to earn it Spider-Rat Queen Fang Plaque Defeat the Spider-Rat Queen Syndicate Ring Display Case Finish Arc 1"},{"p":"Housing","h":"Guests and Roommates","u":"housing.html#guests","x":"Command What it does /apartment invite <name> Lets them visit. /apartment uninvite takes it back. /apartment trust <name> A roommate: they can build and use your chests. /apartment untrust takes it back. /apartment visit <name> Visit someone who invited you. /apartment kick <name> Send a visitor outside. /apartment info Who can visit and who can build."},{"p":"Getting Started","h":"Getting Started","u":"how-to-play.html","x":"How to join Republic City MC and what to do in your first hour. You arrive in the City Hall lobby with no papers. Here's how to get in the game and find your feet. At a glance Edition Java 1.21.11 only Access Beta, whitelist only: DM Hammy on Discord First stop Registrar Huan, City Hall lobby Lost? Hold your quest compass: it shows your task and points the way Contents Joining the Server Your First Hour Origins and Paths Finding Your Way"},{"p":"Getting Started","h":"Joining the Server","u":"how-to-play.html#connect","x":"Server address Address coming soon Copy Java Edition 1.21.11 Beta: whitelist only Checking… Java Edition 1.21.11 only. Bedrock (phone, console, Windows Bedrock) can't join. Make an installation set to 1.21.11: Minecraft Launcher or Modrinth App . Get on the whitelist. The beta is whitelist only: DM Hammy on Discord with your exact Minecraft username. Can't connect? Look your error up in this guide , or ask in the Discord with a screenshot."},{"p":"Getting Started","h":"Your First Hour","u":"how-to-play.html#first-hour","x":"Talk to Registrar Huan behind the brass grille. He hands you a blank Citizen Registration Form. Create your character. Right-click the form: type your character's name in chat (one name, or first and last), pick your Place of Origin and your path , then click Sign & File . Origin and path are permanent; a name change later costs 100 Yuans at City Hall. Check your abilities. Your starting moves are already on your hotbar. /b display lists them; see Commands for the rest. Collect your starter kit from Huan: a training staff, cabbage cookies and the Welcome to Republic City pamphlet. Waterbenders also get water bottles. Follow the story. Huan sends you to your first job. The Main Story page has walkthroughs if you get stuck."},{"p":"Getting Started","h":"Origins and Paths","u":"how-to-play.html#origins","x":"Nation Places of origin Earth Kingdom Ba Sing Se, Omashu, Gaoling, Kyoshi Island, Chin Village Fire Nation Capital City, Ember Island, Shu Jing Water Tribes Northern, Southern, Foggy Swamp United Republic Republic City Any origin can take any path: Earthbender , Waterbender , Firebender , or the two non-bender paths, Chi Blocker and Weapons Master . There are no player airbenders."},{"p":"Getting Started","h":"Finding Your Way","u":"how-to-play.html#finding-your-way","x":"Quest compass. Hold it to see your current task above the hotbar. It points along the streets, not through walls. Markers. A floating ! over someone means they have a job for you; ? means go back and report. Waypoints. Landmarks unlock as you walk past them. /wp takes you back to any you've found. Objectives and rewards. When you finish a step, it flashes on screen along with your next one. Quest Points, Yuans and Order or Chaos show on screen when you earn them."},{"p":"Main Story","h":"Main Story","u":"quests.html","x":"Arc 1 of the Republic City MC story, The Swarm and The Underworld, with spoiler walkthroughs. Arc 1 Title The Swarm & The Underworld Quests 9 in three parts, plus a finale Starts Registrar Huan, City Hall lobby Rewards About 41 QP, 580 Yuans, your own apartment Choices Two Order or Chaos decisions The story starts the moment you walk into City Hall. Spider-Rats in the walls are only the beginning: something is moving under the Civic District, and the Terra Triad is part of it. Walkthroughs are hidden below; open one only if you're stuck. Contents The Three Parts Walkthroughs Achievements"},{"p":"Main Story","h":"The Three Parts","u":"quests.html#parts","x":"Part Quests What happens 1: The Spider-Rat Crisis 1–4 Get registered, help the neighborhood with a Spider-Rat problem, and follow it underground. 2: Finding Your Feet 5–6 Meet the Avatar, learn the Civic District, and prove you can hold your own. 3: The Underworld 7–9 Follow the trail deeper. That's all we'll say. Finishing Arc 1 earns the key to your own room at Unity Flats: see Housing . Want more to do along the way? Try the side quests ."},{"p":"Main Story","h":"Achievements","u":"quests.html#achievements","x":"Each one unlocks a title to wear: see Dossier & Titles . Achievement How to earn it Title Down the Drain Enter the Civic Sewers Tunnel Rat Queen Slayer Defeat the Spider-Rat Queen Nestbane Citizen of the Republic Receive your Citizenship Papers Citizen Civic Defender Finish Arc 1 Civic Defender"},{"p":"Roleplay Ranks","h":"Roleplay Ranks","u":"roleplay-ranks.html","x":"The groups you can join on Republic City MC, who they take, and what it takes to rise. Join a group and climb its ranks with Quest Points, your tier and your alignment . Ranks show on your nametag and your dossier . At a glance When Coming after Arc 1 Groups 8, from the police to the street gangs To join Your tier, Quest Points and alignment Shows on Your nametag and dossier Coming after Arc 1. The groups and requirements below are the plan and may still change. Contents The Groups By Path"},{"p":"Roleplay Ranks","h":"The Groups","u":"roleplay-ranks.html#groups","x":"Group Side Who can join To join Ranks Republic City Police Order Any path Tier II · Order 25 Cadet → Officer → Detective → Chief of Police United Forces Order Any path Tier II · Order 50 Officer → Lieutenant → Captain → Commander White Lotus Order Any path Tier III · Order 100 Initiate → Sentry → Grand Lotus Kyoshi Warriors Order Chi Blocker, Weapons Master Tier II · Order 50 Warrior → Master Fan Dancer Cabbage Corp Neutral Any path Tier I · 50 Yuans Cart Vendor → Warehouse Supervisor → Distribution Manager → Executive Red Lotus Chaos Any path Tier III · Chaos 100 Initiate → Sentry → Grand Lotus The Ungiven Chaos Chi Blocker, Weapons Master Tier II Member → Lieutenant Street Gangs: Terra Triad, Agni Kai, Red Monsoon Chaos Earth, fire or water (one gang each) Tier I · Chaos 25 Grunt → Hitman → Captain → Underboss → Crime Lord"},{"p":"Roleplay Ranks","h":"By Path","u":"roleplay-ranks.html#by-path","x":"Any path: Republic City Police, United Forces, White Lotus, Red Lotus, Cabbage Corp. Chi blockers and weapons masters: also the Kyoshi Warriors and The Ungiven. Benders: also your element's street gang: Terra Triad , Agni Kai or Red Monsoon ."},{"p":"Rules","h":"Rules","u":"rules.html","x":"How the city works in game, and where to find the full server rules. The full server rules are pinned in #rules on our Discord . In game, the city works like this. At a glance Full rules Pinned in #rules on Discord Building Not allowed in the city. Bending is. Your stuff Quest items can't be lost: check /backpack Need staff /helpop <message>"},{"p":"Rules","h":"City Ordinances","u":"rules.html#city","x":"Rule What it means Bend freely, build nothing Bend anywhere in the city. You can't place or break blocks, and bent earth goes back on its own. Doors are private You can't open doors or trapdoors, except where a quest sends you. Bloodbending is a crime Outlawed in 130 AG. It never unlocks. Report Triad activity To Chief Beifong's Metalbending Police. Or don't: see Order & Chaos ."},{"p":"Rules","h":"Your Things Are Safe","u":"rules.html#safety","x":"Quest items can't be dropped. If you die, they go to your /backpack . Lost your papers or form? They come back the next time you log in. Nothing for sale makes you stronger. If a store ever opens, it's cosmetics only."},{"p":"Rules","h":"Getting Help","u":"rules.html#help","x":"Stuck, bugged or need a hand? Use /helpop <message> in game to reach staff, or ask in the Discord."},{"p":"Side Quests","h":"Side Quests","u":"side-quests.html","x":"Optional side quests in Republic City MC: who gives them, when they unlock, and what they pay. Short, optional jobs around the Civic District, each worth Quest Points. Look for a floating ! over the person who needs help. At a glance In Arc 1 7 side quests Find them A floating ! over the person who needs help Track one /quests , then click it All of them 14 QP and 155 Yuans, plus a few keepsakes You can run several at once alongside the main story. /quests (or the Quest Log button on your dossier) lists them all with their rewards; click one to make your quest compass follow it. Contents Available Now Walkthroughs Coming Next"},{"p":"Side Quests","h":"Available Now","u":"side-quests.html#available","x":"Quest Given by Unlocks Reward Scrap Lessons Old Man Shen, market by the Sparring Grounds Once your form is filed 1 QP, 20 Yuans, the basic recipes Tora Lady Shijimi, outside City Hall After Quest 2 2 QP, 25 Yuans The Gutsy Earthbender Author Jira, Republic City Library Any time 2 QP, 20 Yuans, a signed first edition Special Delivery Postmaster Kotetsu, Messenger Hawk Post After Quest 6 2 QP, 20 Yuans, Order or Chaos Rookie on the Beat Officer Izumo, outside Ging's Antiques After Quest 6 2 QP, 25 Yuans Scoop! Reporter Shiho, by the Messenger Hawk Post After Quest 2 2 QP, 20 Yuans, Order or Chaos, a newspaper The Petition Ayame, near Noodle Man Raku's ramen truck After Quest 6 3 QP, 25 Yuans"},{"p":"Side Quests","h":"Coming Next","u":"side-quests.html#coming","x":"More of Republic City, in Arc 2."},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"Waterbending","u":"waterbending.html","x":"Waterbending on Republic City MC: abilities by tier, water sources, ice, healing and plants, trainers and ranks. Waterbending Element Water Style Change: push and pull, turn their force back on them Paths None yet Discipline Ice · Healing · Plant from Tier II Trainers Young Kya · Master Kanok · Katara Strongest At night (+25%) Gang Red Monsoon Waterbenders shape water, ice and the life in plants. They're versatile: attack, defense, movement and healing all come from the same element. You need water to bend water. You start with a few water bottles, and fountains, canals and the bay are all fair game. Contents Abilities What You Can Bend Paths Trainers Roleplay Ranks Tips"},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"Abilities","u":"waterbending.html#abilities","x":"Tier Abilities I · Forms Water Manipulation, Surge, Torrent, Water Spout, Water Bubble II · Street Octopus Form, Phase Change, Ice Spike, Healing Waters, Ice Wave combo III · Master Ice Blast, Ice Bullet combo ★ · Legend Water Arms Combos are performed by chaining other moves; /b help <combo> shows the sequence. What each tier needs: Bending & Tiers ."},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"What You Can Bend","u":"waterbending.html#sources","x":"From tier Sources I Water and snow II Ice, and plants: leaves, grass, flowers, vines, moss, cactus, sugar cane, melons and pumpkins Tier II also opens healing . Ice, healing and plants together are your Discipline on your dossier ."},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"Paths","u":"waterbending.html#paths","x":"Waterbending has no Tier III path yet: every waterbender walks the ice line above. Healer and plant paths will come once there are well-made moves for them. Bloodbending is outlawed in 130 AG and never unlocks."},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"Trainers","u":"waterbending.html#trainers","x":"Tier Trainer II Young Kya Katara's daughter. Exam coming soon. III Master Kanok Northern Tribe diplomat. ★ Katara Master healer."},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"Roleplay Ranks","u":"waterbending.html#ranks","x":"Red Monsoon (Chaos): the waterbender gang. Tier I and 25 Chaos to join. Plus the ranks open to every path: police, United Forces, White Lotus, Red Lotus and Cabbage Corp. See Roleplay Ranks ."},{"p":"Waterbending","h":"Tips","u":"waterbending.html#tips","x":"Keep your water bottles: they're your source anywhere dry. Water Spout and Surge carry you across deep water; Water Bubble keeps the water off you underneath it. You're 25% stronger at night."},{"p":"Weapons Master","h":"Weapons Master","u":"weapons-master.html","x":"The Weapons Master path on Republic City MC: abilities, blades and blueprints, trainers and ranks. Weapons Master Type Non-bender Style Any weapon, real steel Paths Coming later Trainers Young Bumi · Mai · Sokka Blades Blueprints from TenTen Ranks Kyoshi Warriors, The Ungiven Weapons Masters don't bend. Their abilities bind to the hotbar like bending and work with whatever weapon is in hand, using its damage and any special effects it has. Sokka proved a sword and a plan can stand next to the Avatar. Republic City has plenty of people who'd like to prove it again. Contents Abilities Weapons Trainers Roleplay Ranks"},{"p":"Weapons Master","h":"Abilities","u":"weapons-master.html#abilities","x":"Tier Abilities I · Forms Leaping Strike, Weapon Throw, Battle Stance II and up coming later What each tier needs: Bending & Tiers ."},{"p":"Weapons Master","h":"Weapons","u":"weapons-master.html#weapons","x":"Any weapon works, but better blades hit harder. Weapons Vendor TenTen at the Sparring Grounds sells blades, and only Weapons Masters can buy them. You can also craft your own from blueprints: Blueprint Where Simple Jian, Dao, Gaff Hook TenTen, 40 Yuans each Simple Maul TenTen, 60 Yuans Spider Fang Dagger Epic hidden caches only Right-click a blueprint to learn it for good. Recipes and stats: Crafting and the Field Guide ."},{"p":"Weapons Master","h":"Trainers","u":"weapons-master.html#trainers","x":"Tier Trainer II Young Bumi Aang's nonbending son. Exam coming soon. III Mai Precision, stealth and projectiles. ★ Sokka Councilman and strategist."},{"p":"Weapons Master","h":"Roleplay Ranks","u":"weapons-master.html#ranks","x":"Kyoshi Warriors (Order) and The Ungiven (Chaos): chi blockers and weapons masters only. Tier II. Plus the ranks open to every path. See Roleplay Ranks ."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Spider-Rat","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Mei-Lin's apartment (Unity Flats), Civic Sewers. Fast and swims well. Gets a burst of speed when three or more are together. Scatters for a few seconds when a Spider-Rat Soldier dies nearby."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Spider-Rat Soldier","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Jian's Tea Shop cellar, Civic Sewers. Poisonous bite. Enrages below 30% health, gaining Speed and Strength. When it dies, the small Spider-Rats around it run."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Brood Sac","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Civic Sewers (one on each level). Doesn't move. Hatches a Spider-Rat every 10 seconds while you're nearby. Break it and the hatching stops; a new sac grows back after a couple of minutes."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Spider-Rat Queen","u":"field-guide.html#bosses","x":"The Nest, deepest chamber of the Civic Sewers. 90 health solo, more with every extra player (up to 240). Lunges to knock you back. Takes turns between Web Spit (slows you hard for 3 seconds), Summon Brood (3 Spider-Rats) and Brood Swap (trades places with one of her rats). At 40% health she flees to her nest and heals while her brood guards her. At 20% she goes into a frenzy."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Waterbending Police Recruit","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Sparring Grounds. Water Whip: a stream of water that slows you and knocks you back, and can freeze your feet in place. Splash: shoves you back when struck. Yields at low health and gives you a tip."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Earthbending Police Recruit","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Sparring Grounds. Earth Blast: a telegraphed boulder that hits for 5 and knocks you back. Stone Guard: braces behind stone and takes much less damage for a moment, so wait it out. Yields at low health and gives you a tip."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Firebending Police Recruit","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Sparring Grounds. Fire Cone: a short flame burst that sets you alight. Fire Dash: leaps toward you. Sometimes sidesteps a hit completely. Yields at low health and gives you a tip."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Weapons Master Police Recruit","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Sparring Grounds. Fights with an iron sword and lunges at you from close range. Sometimes parries a hit and shoves you back. Yields at low health and gives you a tip."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Terra Triad Grunt","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Terra Triad Bruiser","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Terra Triad Pickpocket","u":"field-guide.html#mobs","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Pitmaster Jax","u":"field-guide.html#bosses","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Street Skewer","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"5 yuan (8 for 40). Noodle Man Raku (ramen truck, Civic Plaza). Restores 4 Hunger. Cheapest meal in the district."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Cabbage Cookie","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"3 yuan (8 for 24). Noodle Man Raku (ramen truck, Civic Plaza). Restores 2 Hunger and gives Speed I for 5s."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Raku's Ramen","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"12 yuan. Noodle Man Raku (ramen truck, Civic Plaza). Restores 10 Hunger. The house specialty. Bowls don't stack."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Kwong's Signature Dish","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"12 yuan. Kwong's Cuisine (Downtown District). Restores 8 Hunger and gives Saturation II."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Bamboo Bundle","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Craft only (4 bamboo cost 6 yuan). Crafting (recipe from Old Man Shen's Scrap Lessons); bamboo from Old Man Shen (market by the Sparring Grounds). Base material for staffs, bows and arrows."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Scrap Steel Ingot","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Craft only (4 iron scrap cost 20 yuan). Crafting (recipe from Old Man Shen's Scrap Lessons); iron scrap from Old Man Shen. Terra Triad Bruisers (5%). Base material for Tier I blades."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Bundle of Arrows (8)","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"18 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Standard arrows."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Bamboo Smoke Bomb","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Craft only. Crafting; Blasting Powder from Old Man Shen (4 yuan). Terra Triad Bruisers (10%). Use it to blind everything within 4 blocks for 5s."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Basic Training Staff","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"30 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Huan's starter kit. 3 damage, 2.2 attack speed. Usable by every path."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Standard Shield","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"45 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Directional blocking."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Standard Bow","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"40 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Legal to carry without a permit."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Concealed Dagger","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"35 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds), or crafting. 4 damage, 2.0 attack speed. High critical hit chance."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Simple Jian","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"65 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds), or craft it with TenTen's blueprint. 5 damage, 1.6 attack speed. Balanced sidearm."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Simple Dao","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"65 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds), or craft it with TenTen's blueprint. 4.6 damage, 1.9 attack speed. Fast close-quarters recovery."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Simple Maul","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"100 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds), or craft it with TenTen's blueprint. 5.4 damage, 1.3 attack speed. Disables shields."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Simple Gaff Hook","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"65 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds), or craft it with TenTen's blueprint. 4.4 damage, 2.0 attack speed. Pulls a target 2 blocks toward you."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Terra Triad Switchblade","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Not sold. Pitmaster Jax (5%). 4.8 damage, 2.1 attack speed. Carrying it openly costs 1 Order point."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Spider Fang Dagger","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Not sold. Crafting, with the blueprint from epic loot chests. 5.5 damage, 1.8 attack speed. Hits apply Poison II for 4s."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Emergency Inspection Dispatch","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Spider-Rat Queen Fang","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Citizenship Papers","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Marked Syndicate Ring","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Spider-Rat Pelt","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Shady Zhen pays 1 yuan. Spider-Rats (35%), Spider-Rat Soldiers (80%), Spider-Rat Queen (100%). Common crafting material from sewer vermin. Used in the Spider Fang Dagger."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Brood Queen Chitin","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Shady Zhen pays 15 yuan. Spider-Rat Queen (25%). Rare trophy needed to forge the Spider Fang Dagger."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Terra Triad Chit","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Terra Triad Vault Seal","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Scroll: Catapult","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Spoiler: open the Field Guide to read it."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Blueprint: Simple Jian","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"40 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Right-click to learn the Simple Jian recipe for good. The blueprint is used up."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Blueprint: Simple Dao","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"40 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Right-click to learn the Simple Dao recipe for good. The blueprint is used up."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Blueprint: Simple Gaff Hook","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"40 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Right-click to learn the Simple Gaff Hook recipe for good. The blueprint is used up."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Blueprint: Simple Maul","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"60 yuan. Weapons Vendor TenTen (Sparring Grounds). Right-click to learn the Simple Maul recipe for good. The blueprint is used up."},{"p":"Field Guide","h":"Blueprint: Spider Fang Dagger","u":"field-guide.html#items","x":"Not sold. Epic loot chests (rare). Right-click to learn the Spider Fang Dagger recipe for good. The blueprint is used up."}];
